NV_PK(11,{"this is shennong street it was once called beishi street in the old five channels harbor area two story old shophouses line the lane with painted lanterns under the roofs":"","this old shophouse has a wooden upper floor with a small wooden window one lantern says five channels the old harbor area this street belonged to":"","this stone tells the story of repairing jinhua temple on beishi street the old name of this street":"","look up a wooden shophouse's second floor hung with painted lanterns":"","this cream colored old house has a curvy red iron balcony bright pink bougainvillea grows beside it":"","at the end of the street stands the medicine king temple it honors shennong in legend he taught people farming and herbal medicine the street was named after this temple which is over three hundred years old":"","shennong street was once beishi street it was renamed after the medicine king temple at its end":""});